WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.120
In a recent interview with Yahoo!

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:06.359
Movies, Thor: Ragnarok writer Eric Pearson
revealed that one planned scene was left on

00:00:06.359 --> 00:00:10.880
the cutting room floor—it was a spaghetti
joke, and it was pretty gross.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.780
We can't count the number of times spaghetti
has shown up as a gag in a movie or show.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.760
Sometimes it's sweet, other times it's a little
more disgusting.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:26.070
But the cut scene in Thor: Ragnarok might
have been the most disgusting of all.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:29.769
Behind the scenes, the writers called it "the
Noodle Worm Scene,'" which should tell you

00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:31.230
how gross it was.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.230
Pearson explained:

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:36.140
"It was an emotional check-in moment with
Bruce Banner and Thor before the finale, with

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.820
Banner eating alien food and trying to be
serious.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:43.920
It [looks like] spaghetti, but then he realizes
the thing he's eating is alive on the end."

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.350
Yup, in this case, "noodle worm" was entirely
literal.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.760
"Please, Nick, eat some busghetti."

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.480
"I didn't realize you enjoyed eating worms!"

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:58.780
So why was the scene cut?

00:00:58.789 --> 00:00:59.809
Pearson went on to say:

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:02.460
"I spent so much time on it, and it just never
made it in.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:05.850
We thought it was this pivotal character moment,
and it never had a place.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:07.380
It crushed the momentum."

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.080
This scene marks yet another moment clipped
from Thor: Ragnarok, which was originally

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:15.110
going to include a second major Thor villain
and feature a flashback scene of a chubby

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:16.619
Thor and an emo Loki.

00:01:30.479 --> 00:01:33.829
Maybe the "noodle worm" will still make an
appearance in a future Thor movie, although

00:01:33.829 --> 00:01:37.130
something tells us you'd never look at a plate
of spaghetti the same way again.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.510
Thanks for watching!

